    "explanation": "Both parties should read this the same way: the record of what happened at Blk 682 Woodlands Ave 6 on 29 July 2026 is clear, but the policy does not let the automated pipeline finish the case.\n\nWHAT THE RECORD SHOWS. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00207) has the driver arriving at 06:41:20 and terminating at 06:49:37 as RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00207) puts him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 06:41:10 and holding still for 507 seconds — 8 min 27 s — against the 300-second minimum, starting from the first qualifying in-geofence fix as POL-NS-01 requires. All four POL-NS-01 conditions therefore hold, and the SGD 4.00 fee is validly chargeable under the fee schedule's greater-of rule (STANDARD zone fee SGD 4.00, RYDE_X tier fee SGD 4.00). The rider's assertion that he came down only a few minutes late is rejected: his own device track in the same trace (118 fixes) sits 1,894–1,907 m from the pin across the whole waiting window, never inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, with zero qualifying presence fixes. POL-NS-04 (rider contact unanswered) cannot apply because the rider sent no locating message; POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) cannot apply because the driver was stationary inside the geofence at the marker; POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) cannot apply because he was inside the arrival radius, not stationary 50–400 m outside it. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is citable but changes nothing: the 507-second hold was a single unbroken run, so POL-NS-06 accumulation never arises and no refund-on-shortfall is available. None of the POL-NS-08(a)–(d) impairments is met (clock agreement within 90 s, no trace gap, 4 chat entries matching the recorded chat count, the SGD 4.00 line reconciling), so no POL-NS-08 escalation applies.\n\nWHY THE CASE STILL GOES TO A HUMAN. POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80% of the fee (SGD 3.20) only if its anti-farming check passes. It does not. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 7 (4 or more) and 7 ÷ 61 completed trips is 11.5%, above the 0.08 threshold; both limbs are met, so compensation is WITHHELD and POL-NS-09(d) makes escalation to a human reviewer mandatory. Escalation is terminal: no money moves, and the SGD 4.00 remains held rather than collected or refunded (the fare record already shows payment_status PENDING and refund_issued_sgd 0.00) while review is pending. The rider's no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 POL-NS-09(d) reads, and disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 for both parties, so no rider-side abuse limb or POL-NS-09(c) conflict is engaged; the escalation rests entirely on the driver's trailing-30-day pattern. That counter is citable for this test only and is not a finding about this trip. The driver's passing reference to the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter was flagged as a context-only field under POL-GEN-01 and was not used as a ground of decision by either side.\n\nTHE OPEN QUESTION AND THE INSTRUCTION THAT RIDES WITH IT. The reviewer must confirm the anti-farming pattern and complete the disposition of the held SGD 4.00. POL-NS-07 directs that the escalation packet instruct the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full, so that the rider does not fund a dispute the platform has not resolved. Confidence is above the 0.70 floor; the deciding facts rest on artifacts of weight 1.0."
