    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver.\n\nOn the merits of the no-show, the driver is right and the rider's claim fails. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00207, weight 1.0, 100% coverage, no gaps) shows the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at Blk 682 Woodlands Ave 6 from 06:41:10, stationary, for one unbroken in-geofence run of 507 seconds, with 52 qualifying in-radius fixes. That is 207 seconds more than the 300-second STANDARD minimum dwell. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00207, weight 1.0) records the arrival marker at 06:41:20 — ten seconds after the first qualifying fix — and records the driver cancelling at 06:49:37 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which is after the dwell elapsed at 06:46:10. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold: (a) an arrival event, (b) in-geofence fixes before it, (c) a continuous qualifying dwell of 507 s against 300 s, (d) no boarding and a driver termination on RIDER_NO_SHOW after the dwell. The SGD 4.00 fee reconciles with the fee schedule's greater-of rule (STANDARD zone-class fee 4.00; RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee 4.00 — it is a tie and the higher figure governs), so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises.\n\nThree clauses that could have displaced that result do not. POL-NS-05 does not catch the arrival marker: at 06:41:20 the driver was inside the geofence and stationary, not more than 300 m from the pin and not travelling at 15 km/h or above, so no recomputation of the waiting clock is required. POL-NS-06 produces no shortfall (507 s against 300 s), and because the hold was a single unbroken run, the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation rule was never needed — so the absence of a traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00207-01, MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is citable but does not change anything; the driver's point on this is accepted. POL-NS-03 is confined to a driver stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin; here the stationary fixes are inside the 50 m radius itself, so there is no mislocation to apportion and no pin-ambiguity goodwill.\n\nThe rider's account is contradicted by his own device. The rider track in EV-GPS-00207 places him between 1,894 m and 1,907 m from the pickup pin across 118 fixes, never once within the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, with zero qualifying presence fixes. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00207, weight 1.0) holds four entries between 06:41:21 and 06:49:20 — one system arrival notice and three messages from the driver, each delivered and each read — and nothing at all from the rider. Limb (a) of POL-NS-04 (a locating or coordinating message from the rider) therefore fails, so that exoneration clause cannot run. The driver's conduct was patient and documented: an unanswered in-app call at 06:45:10 and messages at 06:42:30, 06:46:02 and 06:49:20, before cancelling at 06:49:37.\n\nWhat prevents a ruling in the driver's favour is POL-NS-07's anti-farming check, and both sides accept the arithmetic of it. The driver profile (EV-DPROF-00207, weight 1.0) records 7 no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days against 61 completed trips — at or above 4 terminations, and 11.5%, above the 0.08 threshold. Both limbs are met. The consequence is fixed by the clause: the driver's compensation of SGD 3.20 (80% of the SGD 4.00 fee) is withheld, and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). Those two profile fields are citable under POL-GEN-01 for this test only; the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter was mentioned but expressly not used, and it is not a ground of this decision. No rider-side escalation ground is engaged either: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 that POL-NS-09(d) reads, and neither party's disputes_with_counterparty_90d reaches 2 under POL-NS-09(c).\n\nESCALATE is terminal for the automated pipeline, so no money moves here: amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd are both null, and the disputed SGD 4.00 stays held rather than collected or refunded. The payments ledger already shows that state (payment_status PENDING, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, total_charged 4.50 including the platform fee 0.50). The escalation trigger is the tripped POL-NS-07 anti-farming check under POL-NS-09(d). The open question the human reviewer must settle is the anti-farming review of driver DRV-01948's trailing-30-day termination pattern and any account-level action it warrants. The refund itself is not an open question: under POL-NS-07 the escalation packet directs the reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in full, and that reference is carried in referrals."
